    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327-a1">

                <pb facs="0364" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg274"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Balfour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Ambassador at Washington</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Czechs at Vladivostok. We trust that the United States Government will give
                    authority to the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> to support the
                    Czechs in case of necessity. Without going into the wider question of Allied
                    intervention, it is certain that a most serious effect would everywhere be
                    produced if the Czechs at Vladivostok were to suffer a collapse which could in
                    any way be attributed to a failure on the part of the Allies to give them
                    support.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
